<section class="training-section methodology-section">

    <div class="bg-animation">
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
    </div>

    <h2 class="section-title">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-chalkboard-user title-icon"></i> Teaching Methodology
    </h2>

    <div class="methodology-container">

        <div class="methodology-intro">
            <p>
                All the programs are designed to suit the professional needs of an individual trainee
                and also an individual organization.
            </p>

            <p>
                Students are encouraged to develop a critical and analytical approach to what they
                study in the classroom. WQC believes the transfer of learning from classroom to
                practical workstation is the hallmark of quality education.
            </p>

            <p>
                FCES employees arrange effective methodology to ensure quality learning.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="methodology-grid">

            <div class="method-card">
                <h3>  <i class="fa-solid fa-graduation-cap icon-animate"></i> Teaching Methods</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li> <i class="fa-solid fa-person-chalkboard"></i> Classroom teaching by eminent faculty involving lectures, PowerPoint presentations and handouts.</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-people-arrows"></i>  Stimulated situations and role-plays to understand industry responsibilities.</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Workshops to analyse real practical situations.</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-computer"></i> Access to institute computers and internet facilities.</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-book-open"></i> Case studies to understand industry processes.</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa-solid fa-industry"></i> Industrial visits for practical exposure.</li>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-briefcase"></i> Industrial internship programs.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="method-card">
                <h3> <i class="fa-solid fa-chart-line icon-animate"></i> Assessment & Delivery Strategy</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><i class="fa-solid fa-comments"></i> Learners receive feedback on their progress throughout the course.</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa-solid fa-oil-can"></i> Delivery strategies reflect real employment conditions in the Oil and Gas Industry.</li>
                    <li> <i class="fa-solid fa-flask"></i>Students complete assessments in real or simulated industry environments.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

</section>




<!-- MENTORSHIP -->
<section class="training-section alt-bg">

    <h2 class="section-title" data-aos="fade-up">Student Mentorship Program</h2>

    <p class="mentor-intro" data-aos="fade-up">
        We at FCES believe in providing education aligned with international standards through classroom
        training and continuous interaction with industry professionals. This initiative helps students
        develop professional excellence in technical skills and real-world industry exposure.
    </p>

    <div class="mentor-grid">

        <div class="mentor-card" data-aos="zoom-in">
            <h4 class="icon-title">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-bullseye"></i>
            Objective</h4>
            <p>
                The program empowers students with live functional experiences from industry experts,
                helping them become more adaptable to professional requirements.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mentor-card" data-aos="zoom-in">
            <h4 class="icon-title">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-user-tie"></i>
            About Mentorship</h4>

            <ul>
                <li>Students connect with function-specific industry experts during their program.</li>
                <li>Helps combine classroom knowledge with real life learning.</li>
                <li>Students meet mentors every month for guidance.</li>
                <li>Learning reports must be submitted within 7 days of the meeting.</li>
                <li>Meeting agenda and learning goals are finalized with faculty beforehand.</li>
                <li>Faculty evaluates student learning and assigns performance marks.</li>
            </ul>

        </div>

        <div class="mentor-card" data-aos="zoom-in">
            <h4 class="icon-title">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-chalkboard-user"></i>
            Benefits to Mentor</h4>

            <ul>
                <li>Share professional knowledge with future engineers.</li>
                <li>Contribute to the noble cause of education.</li>
                <li>Receive recognition as adjunct (visiting) faculty.</li>
            </ul>

        </div>

        <div class="mentor-card" data-aos="zoom-in">
            
            <h4 class="icon-title">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-user-graduate"></i>
                Benefits to Student
            </h4>

            <ul>
                <li>Connect classroom learning with real industry situations.</li>
                <li>Gain practical insights from experienced professionals.</li>
                <li>Enhance professional growth and career readiness.</li>
            </ul>

        </div>

    </div>

</section>
